# item27m: Banque01 story route, walked. Replaces the item27l route's remaining teleports where
# the decoded engine behavior measurably supports the walk; any kept teleport carries a measured
# cause. Objective 0 "Access the strongroom." completes through the game's own chain (Cine15
# Jones scene -> `event fin_flash` -> XIIIDispatcher4 -> GT_quitterbanque -> XIIIGoalTrigger0) and
# objective 1 "Escape from the bank." through Cine11's `playerevent fin_map` -> XIIIGoalTrigger2
# -> DoTravel -> Amos01, exactly as in item24/item27k/item27l.
#
# item27m teleport-1 fix (the t=13 key spot): Engine.dll execCanSee (0x1036f070) -> SeePawn
# (0x1036dc40) -> LineOfSightTo (0x1036ac70) decoded; the VM now traces the engine's lines (base
# Location first, then the Enemy eye point without distance limits or the 0.8*CollisionHeight top
# with 8000^2/2000^2 limits) and applies SeePawn's SightRadius/Visibility range gate. Unit tests
# in crates/xiii-script/src/vm_tests.rs (line_of_sight_to_*, can_see_*); the customer-side release
# measured in local/re/item27m/probe-customer.log. The t=13 teleport is GONE.
#
# Walked story chain (all measured in probe-u/probe-t runs, cine trace):
#   - spawn -> DetectionVolume1 (touch starts Cine1, the teller scene).
#   - walk to the counter spot (-330,-2133): Cine1[12] "wait player 300" (vs the teller at
#     (-494,-2133)) passes; the customer queue maze is walkable (probe-m).
#   - Cine1[16] "wait event recoit_cle" then needs Banque0.STA_DonneCle.Tick to see
#     VSize2D(teller-player)<300 && CanSee(teller). From the customer side CanSee measurably
#     fails (the counter blocks the eye line; probe-m sat at (-330,-2133) for 10+ s with no
#     release), and the staff side is sealed by Porte7 until the teller herself opens it at
#     action[29] — which requires recoit_cle. Measured cause for the ONE remaining lobby
#     teleport: spot E (-494,-2383), the only position that releases the key.
#   - walk the staff corridor north to (-540,-1350): the teller's Cine1[32] "wait player 500"
#     (vs her at (-567,-1284) after `opendoor porte7`) passes.
#   - walk west to (-1560,-1290) and WAIT: the double armored door XIIIMover14/15
#     ("bankporteblindee1") opens only for the teller's Cine1[39] `playerevent porteblindee1`
#     (t~37.4); pushing it earlier wedges (probe-t v2).
#   - follow the teller's own measured waypoints down the stair corridor ((-1717,-1440) ->
#     (-1772,-1940) -> (-1818,-2250), z 107 -> -149): Cine1[43] "wait player 1500", Cine6[4]
#     "wait player 700" (James at (-1859,-2574)) and Cine1[51] "wait player 400" (vs the teller
#     at (-1974,-2418)) all pass on foot. Her chain then fires `event coffre`/`event choatoi`
#     (the vault key), `event toto` (t~50.6, unlocks the vault door Porte8) and Cine6[17]
#     `event coffreserrure` (t~53.7) which OPENS Porte12 (the "coffreentree" door, alpha 0.946
#     by t~59.5) — the item27k-era blocker, gone because the player stays with her.
#   - walk the whole vault corridor on foot: through Porte12, down the ramp to z=-149, around
#     the bankescaroulant block (east side), south along x~=-2300, west along y~=-6100, to the
#     vault door (-2840,-6397). Touches fire the game's own actors: Porte12, Trigger15,
#     BreakableMover0, Porte8, TriggerSound6/11/14, XIIIMover6/27, and XIIIDispatcher5 (the
#     briefcase `debut_flash` chain); Porte20/21 (the vault door panels) open by themselves.
#     The t=44 vault teleport of the old route is gone entirely.
#   - Teleport to DetectionVolume12 (-7616,-2784,1456) — measured cause: there is NO floor
#     connection between the vault level (z=-174 feet) and the strongroom (z 838-1456): the
#     basement corridor terminates at x~=-3550 (slices in local/re/item27l/), the original nav
#     graph has NO PATH for that leg (local/re/item27l/plan-paths.txt leg 5), and probing east
#     along the strongroom platform descends the interior stair and wedges at x~=-7010
#     (local/re/item27m/probe-j.log). No map actor relocates the player either: the flash chain's
#     SoundFlashOn/Off receivers are TriggerSound cues and DV12's Event is 'jones_dial' (starts
#     the Jones dialogue, not a move). The game's own bomb-flash transition covers the move in
#     the original; the teleport delivers DV12's own engine Touch, which fires 'jones_dial'.
#   - walk the strongroom interior: fall from the DV12 platform to the safe level (z=875,
#     Cine15[3] "wait player 300" vs Jones at the safe passes at (-7161,-2141)), then walk the
#     walkway to (-7883,-2648) where Cine15[34] "wait player 300" passes (Jones at
#     (-7885,-2647,875)). Both t=48/t=70 teleports of the old route are gone.
#   - the escape TouchTriggers stay teleports — measured causes (item27m): the volumes are
#     cutscene beats off the AI nav graph (plan-paths.txt leg 8 has NO PATH walkway -> TT5).
#     TT5's spot lands on a terrace whose south edge blocks all movement at y~-2046
#     (probes k/l: the player wedges at (1170..1330,-2046,1322) with southward velocity); the
#     TT2 spot's landing wedges at x~964 with the parking floor ~800 UU below and no measured
#     route down (probe-m); TT3/TT4/TT10 are the fbi_dial2/arrivee_amos/CarOut cutscene beats.
#     Engine notes decoded this round: TriggerEvent is TAG-matched (engine.Actor.TriggerEvent
#     foreaches DynamicActors(.., EventName)); XIIIMover26 (bankmurcoffreKsable, Tag
#     'explocoffre_bis') has no sender anywhere in the map data, and Trigger27 ('bombe',
#     OtherTriggerTurnsOn) has Event=None so its Touch fires nothing — no hidden exit opens
#     after fin_flash. Each teleport delivers the volume's own engine Touch, the game's own code.

